<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The hardened runtime gates Apple Event *sending* on its own, separately
	     from TCC: without this the events fail errAEEventNotPermitted (-1743)
	     and the Automation prompt never even appears, which looks exactly like
	     a broken Spotify. Senders: NowPlayingSource (Spotify, Music),
	     ObsidianVault (Safari, Chrome), QuickLaunch (Terminal). -->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- The CoreAudio process tap reads other processes' output, which the
	     runtime treats as audio capture even though the TCC service it prompts
	     for is AudioCapture (Privacy & Security -> Audio Recording), not
	     Microphone. Without this the tap builds and delivers silence, and a
	     frozen wave reads as a rendering bug. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- Deliberately absent:
	     - App Sandbox. Half of what this app does is impossible inside a
	       container: the CGEvent key tap, a process tap of another app's audio,
	       and reading Safari's window through the Accessibility API.
	     - cs.disable-library-validation. Library validation only refuses code
	       signed by a different Team ID; the two dlopen targets
	       (DisplayServices, login.framework) are Apple platform binaries, so
	       they load fine and this would weaken the app for nothing.
	     - cs.allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory. Nothing here JITs.
	     - get-task-allow. Notarization rejects it outright, and a Release build
	       signed with the free team's "Apple Development" identity *does*
	       carry it: automatic signing issues a development profile that grants
	       it, whatever the configuration says. Confirmed on this build —
	         codesign -d --entitlements - --xml CoteDOs.app | plutil -p -
	       lists it today. Switching CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY to "Developer ID
	       Application" and exporting with method=developer-id drops it. Check
	       the artifact before every submission; the configuration alone does
	       not settle this one. -->
</dict>
</plist>
